#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage=For a spell we done pretty well. Then there came a '''reg'lar''' terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|military}} Permanently organised; being part of a set professional body of troops. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{ant|en|irregular}}
